  "notes": "West leads the ♦8 against 4♥. South has 6 heart tricks, the ♣A, and at least 2 diamond tricks after the opening lead. East will not play the ♦K at trick 1 which would make the contract easy. South needs to develop 1 more trick.\n\nAs dummy has only 1 entry, it would be a mistake to play the ♦2 at trick 1. South would then be held to 2 diamond tricks. The contract would depend on the position of the ♠A.\n\nSouth can guarantee the contract by winning with the ♦A at trick 1. After drawing trump (making sure to preserve the ♥A in dummy), South surrenders a diamond trick.\n\nThe defense may be able to take 2 spade tricks, but dummy now contains 2 winning diamonds on which South can discard his club losers. North has the ♥A as an entry to the long diamonds.",
